  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sri Balkishan Tak vs State Of A.P. And Another on 1 July, 2024 1 The Honourable Sri Justice K.Surender Criminal Revision Case No.1444 Of 2009 Judgment:",
    "facts": "4. The case of P.W.1, who is the Food Inspector is that he was authorized to lift various food samples and accordingly on 23.11.2005, he went to shop premises of the revision petitioner. While he was conducting business, P.W.1 found 3kgs. of laddu that was prepared and kept for sale. On suspicion that the laddus would have been adulterated, he purchased 500 gms. of laddu and sent them to Public Analyst. Formalities meant for sampling and other procedure was followed. Thereafter, P.W.1 received the report of the Analyst, in which the opinion was given that sample do not confirm to the standards of maximum limit of permitted synthetic food colour. Thereafter, notice was sent. After following the due procedure, complaint was filed. 5. Both the Courts below found favour with the case of the Food Inspector that the there was adulterated colour used in preparation of laddus. The said adulteration was that though synthetic food colour was permitted, it did not confirm to the prescribed standards of the colour used.",
